1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:03,300
Lifting on 5 Hours of Sleep
Kills Your Gains

2
00:00:03,250 --> 00:00:07,522
You’re lifting heavy and
eating clean, but your
physique hasn’t changed in
months.

3
00:00:07,522 --> 00:00:12,590
You think you need to train
harder—yet you're ignoring
the biological sabotage
inside your blood.

4
00:00:12,590 --> 00:00:17,909
Every time you cut your
sleep to five hours, you
pull the emergency brake on
your hormone production.

5
00:00:17,909 --> 00:00:24,784
In a JAMA clinical study,
men sleeping five hours a
night saw their testosterone
crash by fifteen percent in
just seven days.

6
00:00:24,784 --> 00:00:28,965
That is biologically
equivalent to aging fifteen
years in one week!

7
00:00:28,965 --> 00:00:30,227
Why?

8
00:00:30,227 --> 00:00:34,795
Because your body only
releases Luteinizing Hormone
during deep slow-wave sleep.

9
00:00:34,795 --> 00:00:39,011
Cut your sleep, and your
brain stops signaling to
produce testosterone.

10
00:00:39,011 --> 00:00:46,068
Worse, your cortisol spikes
by thirty percent—blocking
your androgen receptors and
cannibalizing muscle tissue
for emergency fuel.

11
00:00:46,068 --> 00:00:49,602
Lifting tears down your
muscle; sleep is what
rebuilds it.

12
00:00:49,602 --> 00:00:54,147
Prioritize seven to eight
hours tonight, or your
workout is working against
you.

13
00:00:54,147 --> 00:00:56,386
Subscribe for more science.
